    {
      "sampleKey": "shapes",
      "sampleSet": "living-folio-overview-v1",
      "schemaVersion": 2,
      "type": "Sketch",
      "title": "A thought in two shapes",
      "description": "A circle, a square, and the questions that appear where they meet.",
      "originalDate": "2026-11-05",
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "attrs": {
          "annotations": {
            "drawing": {
              "id": "drawing",
              "kind": "side",
              "text": "The latest published sketch also appears in the homepage margin.",
              "label": "From the sketchbook",
              "showLabel": true
            }
          }
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sample524032a23c61455b935fde442c799ddc",
              "annotations": []
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Illustrative sample writing for exploring this website.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sample124a0b539db940709d1ce340f9c134b8",
              "annotations": [],
              "src": "data:image/png;base64,",
              "alt": "A cobalt circle and square overlap, crossed by pale diagonals and dotted axes, with a small arrow and hand-drawn marks.",
              "caption": "Study 01 · A thought in two shapes. Original geometric drawing made for this prototype."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sample4516c9efb8754ed4829b2d2ab08d84a4",
              "annotations": [
                "drawing"
              ]
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The circle offers one kind of boundary; the square offers another. Neither is more complete. The interesting part is what becomes visible when they share the same centre."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sampleacca7cf3ad894cd7bfa379e53ad487b4",
              "annotations": []
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I drew the diagonals last. They make the centre feel like an answer, although the drawing began as a question. Next time I might leave them out."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sample20443dbaaa9145939f2c0404b463116a",
              "annotations": []
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A drawing does not always need to illustrate a thought that already exists. Sometimes it is how the thought arrives."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "paragraphs": [],
      "notes": [],
      "connected": [
        "woodpecker",
        "notebook"
      ],
      "published": null,
      "dirty": false
    },
    {
      "sampleKey": "draft",
      "sampleSet": "living-folio-overview-v1",
      "schemaVersion": 2,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "A thought I’m not ready to finish",
      "description": "An unpublished sample draft, visible only in the Writing Room.",
      "originalDate": "2026-11-06",
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "attrs": {
          "annotations": {}
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sample7fb5806c928d45a5b9ab0b728dd5a5e6",
              "annotations": []
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Unpublished sample draft.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "sample059de33d018f4c3ba75f88763c221d75",
              "annotations": []
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Perhaps a personal website should be allowed to change its mind. I have not worked out the next sentence yet."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "blockId": "samplefa59518f4f634ea79b5a48ec2befed41",
              "annotations": []
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This page is deliberately left unpublished so you can compare writing, previewing, and publishing."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "paragraphs": [],
      "notes": [],
